  "scope": "Actual original ggml F32 Neg GPU dispatch, default CPU Exp and original CPU join, same 4M inputs, one active slot, one warm then fixed eight diagnostic replays per graph insertion order, on Windows RTX4070 and Air M4 Vulkan. Same ordinary two-slot/65-step changed-input and cancellation/close oracle checks pass on both machines. No P1 or complete G09 gate verdict.",
  "attribution": "Existing public loader_path points to a test-local transparent forwarding loader. Device logical create retains all original features/queues/pNext and additionally enables only a supported calibrated-timestamps extension. Original generated neg_f32_data source+SHA are bound; its reference is cold transformed by the locked ggml float-controls algorithm for actual Vulkan12 RTE/DenormPreserve FP16 flags. Full final bytes and length must match original vkCreateShaderModule, then original pipeline/main, bind, CmdDispatch and actual QueueSubmit ownership are tracked. No recorder-only hook or replacement math.",
  "clock": "Windows actual DEVICE+QPC, actual 10MHz QPC; Air actual DEVICE+MONOTONIC_RAW ns. Each replay retains before/after calibrated raw ticks, maxDeviation, timestampPeriod/validBits, signed modular differences, observed offset drift and conservative mapped envelope. Full GPU bracket must lie inside the actual CPU Exp executor episode after uncertainty and 1us diagnostic guard. Same-phase joins remain after GPU completion. This observed two-calibration model is not a statistical or universal drift/timestamp confidence guarantee.",
  "query_lifetime": "Bounded 512 timestamp queries, distinct pairs per original recording, reset in that original command buffer on replay; only one live slot is observed. Attribution occurs at original submit, availability is read only after original checked completion without extra host WAIT, pool is destroyed at original device destruction after original work owners retire. Copy/other shaders are forwarded without a false Neg identity.",
